            {
              "subject_id": "car"
            },
            {
              "text": " emerges from the deepest part of the shadow, moving straight forward. Its body reads as a low, broad silhouette; the hood stays smooth and level, the roofline is barely distinct, and the wheels turn slowly enough to be seen individually against the dark ground. Faint highlights gather along the leading edge, then slide across the hood and fenders as the vehicle clears the heaviest shadow. The car does not swerve or change speed abruptly; its path stays centered and deliberate. As it advances, the surrounding darkness opens into a graded field of charcoal and near-black, revealing a flat, unmarked surface under the tires and a low, indistinct background behind the vehicle. The tires carry a thin rim of reflected light, while the rear of the car remains partly veiled in shadow. By the end, the car is visibly present in the near-middle distance, still dark and simple in form, and the space around it has resolved enough to separate the moving vehicle from the night."
